{title: 072 - Creator of the Stars of Night}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #072 • CONDITOR ALME • 7.8.8.8}
{lyricist: Anon. Latin, 9th century}
{composer: Sarum Plainsong}
{key: Eb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 72}
{meta: tune CONDITOR ALME}
{meta: meter 7.8.8.8}
{meta: category Trinity - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Gm]Creator [Eb/G]of the [Cm]stars of night,
[Eb]Thy people's [Ab]ever [Bb7]lasting light,
[Eb]O Christ, [Fm]Thou Savior [Eb/Bb]of [Bb]us [Cm]all,
[Cm]We [Ab/C]pray [Bb/F]Thee, [Fm]hear [Ab]us [Fm/Ab]when [Gm]we call.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Gm]At [Eb/G]the great name [Cm]of Jesus, [Eb]now
[Eb]All knees [Ab]must bend, [Bb7/Ab]all hearts [Eb/Bb]must [Bb7]bow;
[Eb]And things [Fm]celestial [Eb/Bb]Thee [Bb]shall [Cm]own,
[Cm]And [Ab/C]things [Bb/F]terrestial, [Fm/Ab]Lord [Gm]alone.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Gm]To [Eb/G]God the Father, [Cm]God the [Eb]Son,
[Eb]And God [Ab]the Spirit, [Bb7]Three [Eb/Bb]in [Bb7]one,
[Eb]Laud, honor, [Fm]might, [Bb7]and [Eb/Bb]glory [Cm]be
[Cm]From age [Ab/C]to [Bb/F]age [Fm]eternally. [Gm]Amen.
{end_of_verse}
